Remove obsolete section definition

The legacy ".text.init" section flag syntax (#alloc, #execinstr) is no
longer understood by modern binutils, so building with newer binutils
fails with:

  arch/arm64/mm/proc.S:189: Error: junk at end of line, first unrecognized character is `#'

Upstream Linux removed this line in commit f00083cae331 ("arm64: mm:
place __cpu_setup in .text"): the ".text.init" section name was legacy
and unused elsewhere, so the section assignment is dropped entirely and
__cpu_setup simply lives in .text. Do the same here.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/proc.S b/arch/arm64/mm/proc.S
index 387976102e14..4770b5078645 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/proc.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/proc.S
@@ -186,8 +186,6 @@
 	ret
 ENDPROC(cpu_do_switch_mm)
 
-	.section ".text.init", #alloc, #execinstr
-
 /*
  *	__cpu_setup
  *
